@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+---
+id: task-005-add-createpatch-to-produce-a-minimal-json-patch-between-two-documents
+type: task
+title: "Add createPatch to produce a minimal JSON Patch between two documents"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Our clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document, instead of the whole
+new version. Export `createPatch(from, to)` from `src/index.ts`: it returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that
+turns `from` into `to` when applied. It must not mutate either input. The patch describes what changed and
+nothing more: when two versions differ in one small place, the patch must be small, not the whole document.
+
+## Design
+
+Recorded in dl-009 (a minimal patch from a recursive diff: members of objects compared one by one, arrays
+aligned by their unchanged elements, and a whole-document `replace` only when the root types differ) and
+dl-010 (the inputs are never mutated, values in the patch are copies, and no error is thrown for JSON
+values). Both are submitted and wait for approval.
+
+## What was done
+
+- `test/create-patch.test.ts`: written first, and run before the implementation existed, where it failed with
+  "does not provide an export named 'createPatch'". It covers equal values, object members (replace, add,
+  remove, nested, escaped names, `__proto__`), array insert, remove and reorder, a root type change, round
+  trips through `applyPatch`, small patches for one change in a 1000-record document, a large array with
+  many changes (past the alignment limit), and the no-mutation and no-sharing guarantees.
+- `src/index.ts`: `createPatch` with a recursive diff: `diffObject`, `diffArray` (common prefix and suffix
+  trimmed, then the middle aligned by a longest common subsequence, and the gaps paired by position),
+  `alignElements` (bounded by `MAX_ALIGNMENT_PAIRS`), and `childPointer` (escapes `~` and `/`). Values in
+  the patch are copied with `structuredClone`, as dl-010 requires.
+- `README.md`: a short section on `createPatch`, with its example checked by running it.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm test`: 135 of 135 pass (103 existing, 32 new).
+- `tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` (TypeScript 5.9.3, strict mode, from outside the repo): no errors.
+- A randomized check outside the repo: 3000 random pairs of documents, each patch applied with `applyPatch`
+  gives back `to`, and neither input changes.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- `jsonEqual` compares objects by their own keys, so two non-JSON objects with no keys (for example two
+  `Date`s) are treated as equal. dl-006 covers rejecting non-JSON input.
+- Arrays with more than `MAX_ALIGNMENT_PAIRS` (1,000,000) element pairs in the changed part are paired by
+  position, so their patches can be longer than the minimum.
+
+## Open
+
+- Whether `createPatch` should reject non-JSON input waits for dl-006.
+
+## Open
+
+- Whether `createPatch` should reject non-JSON input (dl-006 is still pending for `applyPatch`).
